# Copyrighted assets (hard stop)

Never commit Nintendo IP or ROM-derived files. No exceptions: not CI, LFS, "user said add the ROM", bug repro, or embedding as C arrays / headers / base64.

Do not stage:

- `*.sfc` `*.smc` `*.ips` `*.bps` `zelda3_assets.dat`
- `tables/` repo-root `msu/` `sprites-gfx/`
- extract dumps: overworld/dungeon yaml, `assets/img/`, `assets/sprites/*.png`, `assets/sound/`, dialogue, fonts, `linksprite.png`, `hud_icons.png`, `map32_to_map16.txt`, `music_info.yaml`, `sfx.txt`, `sound_*.txt`, `generated_*.h`, `*.pcm` `*.brr` `*.spc`

Do not paste ROM bytes, map16 tables, or ripped graphics into commits, PRs, or issue text.

Before every commit:

```sh
bash scripts/check-no-copyrighted-assets.sh
```

If it is not `OK`, unstage and stop. Never `git add -A`, `git add .`, `git add -f`, or `--no-verify`. Stage named source paths only.
